    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d787">

                <pb facs="0642" n="526" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg526"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/23469.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Special Commissioners to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Niagara Falls</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-06-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 11, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>We have just returned from a meeting of the Mediators Which began with the
                    discussion of Paragraph 1, as to the transfer of power.* * * As a result of a
                    lengthy conference it was substantially agreed that Paragraph 1 should read as
                    follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Paragraph 1. A Provisional Government for the United Mexican States,
                            constituted as hereinafter provided, shall be recognized at Mexico City
                            at noon on the day____of___, 1914, at which time it shall assume and
                            thereafter exercise governmental powers until the election and
                            inauguration of a constitutional president.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>It is proposed that this paragraph be protocolized tomorrow, the Mediators
                    claiming that the only way to make progress is to put <pb facs="0643" n="527"
                        xml:id="pg527"/> in definite and final form what has been agreed upon by
                    both parties, and unless you object we will enter the meeting and agree to the
                    protocolization of the above, for which we have been contending for ten days.
                    While the language is somewhat different, we think it carries out in substance
                    and detail our understanding of the views of the President.* * *</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Commissioners</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
